Return one result for the trial:
- label: positive (the primary outcome differed significantly in favour of the intervention against its comparator) | null (no significant difference) | negative (significantly worse with the intervention) | mixed (several primary outcomes or arms disagree) | not_applicable (no comparison to test: single arm, feasibility, pharmacokinetics, or the primary outcome is a description, not an effect) | not_reported (the sources do not give the primary outcome result);
- source: the id in square brackets of the source you quote;
- quote: one or two consecutive sentences, or one line of a results table, copied exactly, character for character, from that source, that state the primary outcome result; "" when not_reported;
- note: one short line on anything that made the label uncertain (which outcome is primary, comparator, significance not stated), or "".
Significance means the trial's own test (a p-value below its threshold, a confidence interval excluding no effect, or an explicit statement); a numerical difference alone is not significance.

